<title>USA: Seagate enters mid-range tape market.</title>
<headline>Seagate enters mid-range tape market.</headline>
<dateline>COSTA MESA, Calif. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagate Technology Inc said Monday it has entered the mid-range server backup market with a new product called Sidewinder 50.</p>
<p>The new product is a high-performance tape drive based on Advanced Intelligent Tape technology standard from Sony Corp. The Sidewinder 50 has a capacity of up to 50 Gbytes with data compression and transfers data at up to 6 Mbytes per second. The new product is expected to be available in third quarter of 1997.</p>
</text>
